# Straight-line fit to 40 noisy points

## Task and data
Fit a line to n = 40 points, x = 0, 1, ..., 39, y = 2.5 + 0.8 x + e, with e ~ N(0, 3^2) drawn from `numpy.random.default_rng(216)` (one call `rng.normal(0, 3, size=40)`, numpy 2.4.6). The data are determined by the seed together with the numpy version (numpy does not guarantee `default_rng` streams across versions; the versions used are recorded in `results/fit.json`: Python 3.11.2, numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.17.1); they are written to [`results/data.csv`](../results/data.csv). The true parameters (slope 0.8, intercept 2.5, sigma 3) are known only because the data are synthetic; they were not used in the fit.

## Method
Ordinary least squares. Standard errors come from the residual SD s = sqrt(RSS / 38) (n - 2 = 38 degrees of freedom). 95% confidence intervals are estimate +/- t(0.975, 38) x SE with t = 2.0244, which assumes normal errors (true here by construction). The hand-written estimates were asserted equal to `scipy.stats.linregress` in the code. Code: [`code/fit.py`](../code/fit.py) (produces `results/fit.json` and `results/data.csv`); figure code: [`figures/make_fit.py`](../figures/make_fit.py).

## Results
All numbers are from [`results/fit.json`](../results/fit.json).

| Parameter | Estimate | SE | 95% CI | True value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Slope | 0.7206 | 0.0422 | [0.6352, 0.8061] | 0.8 |
| Intercept | 4.3727 | 0.9565 | [2.4364, 6.3090] | 2.5 |

Residual SD = 3.0816 (true sigma 3), R^2 = 0.8847.

